                <pb facs="0274" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg268"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April 2,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your two dispatches of the
                    9th ultimo, relative to the disturbances at the Mosquito Reservation, stating
                    that this Government has not failed to take the action which appeared proper to
                    the end of protecting American interests there.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
